      "worked_solution": "Remember that in general, a negative exponent can be converted to a positive exponent if we take the reciprocal. Here, we have:\n\n$$\n(5k)^{-1/3}=\\frac{1}{(5k)^{1/3}}\n$$\n\nNow, we can proceed as usual to convert the fractional exponent to a radical:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{(5k)^{1/3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{5k}}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n(5k)^{-1/3}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{5k}}\n$$",
